  "narrative": "This account looks fine on revenue (down a mild 13%) but is leaking heavily through discounting: average discount roughly quadrupled to 20% and margin rate has held near 15-16% for eleven straight months versus a 26% baseline. The step is sudden, persistent and broad across categories, not a seasonal dip, so it reads as a structural pricing problem rather than a temporary lull. No single category or tier explains it, so treat it as an account-level discounting issue.",
  "attributed_categories": [],
  "cited_evidence": [
    "Average discount jumped from about 5% to roughly 20% starting October 2025 and has stayed there for eleven straight months.",
    "Margin rate fell from 29.8% in September 2025 to 17.2% the next month and has held near 15-16% since, versus a 26.2% baseline.",
    "Monthly margin in rupees dropped from about \u20b952,504 to about \u20b928,660, even though revenue only slipped 13.0% from baseline.",
    "Revenue decline is mild (13% below baseline, within the account's normal swing) and no single category has stopped buying.",
    "Product declines are spread across five categories (Power Tools, Fasteners, Electrical Accessories, Precision Hardware, Consumables), not concentrated in one."
  ],
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Review the pricing/discount approval on this account's orders since October 2025.",
